<title>USA: Fed stays out of money mkt at intervention time.</title>
<headline>Fed stays out of money mkt at intervention time.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve remained out of the banking system during its usual midmorning intervention time Thursday. The lack of action was not unexpected, though some economists thought reserves could be added.</p>
<p>Fed funds were trading at 5-3/16 percent.</p>
<p>(( -- John P. Hughes, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1663 ))</p>
